// Test: bugfixes/bare_pow_is_not_a_builtin
// Semantic: SEM002 — `pow(...)` is not in the standard library; the spec form is the `^` operator
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.190
// Fixed: 0.33.195 reports an undefined function as SEM002 (semantic-rules.md SEM002), was SEM007
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   SEM002
//   Function 'pow' not found
//
// Regression (#51): the resolver registered a bare `pow` built-in that no
// code generator implements. It passed type checking and then failed with an
// internal "not found in function map" error without an error code (or, for
// `toString`, compiled to an identity function that printed an empty string).

start:
	print(pow(2.0, 3.0))
